  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Login Page**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the login page design. The visual concept centers around a light grey background with a white, rounded card containing the login elements. I\'m thinking of using `bg-slate-50` for the background and a white block with a faint shadow. The logo will be a green square with rounded corners, featuring the initials \'DP\'.\n\n\n**Defining the Input Fields**\n\nI\'ve decided on the input fields for the \"IA Quality Assurance Portal\" login: \"ENTER TEACHER CODE\" and \"ENTER PASSWORD,\" with a \"LOGIN\" button. The title and subtitle are also finalized. I\'m leaning toward a green background for the login button and a night mode toggle. I need to make the mockup secure-ish by doing the password checking server-side. I\'ll use hardcoded teacher codes and a password from my input data.\n\n\n**Refining Login Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the login mechanism. Initially, I considered a `/api/login` endpoint, but opted for a simpler client-side approach given the short list of teacher codes and the nature of the application. I will be using client-side state in `App.tsx` for login determination. The current implementation uses a hardcoded list of teacher codes and a password. I\'m focusing on visual matching, choosing a sans-serif font and considering `bg-emerald-500` for the logo\'s background. I\'m planning to abstract the moderation UI into a separate component, or conditionally return the Login UI if not logged in.\n\n\n**Refactoring Application Structure**\n\nI\'m now refactoring the application. Given file size considerations, I\'ve decided to split `App.tsx` into `Login.tsx` and `Dashboard.tsx`. Specifically, I\'ve created `src/components/Dashboard.tsx` from the existing `App.tsx` return statement, and a new `src/components/Login.tsx`. I\'m updating `App.tsx` to manage the `isLoggedIn` and `teacherCode` states and conditionally render either the login or dashboard components based on state. I\'m focusing on simplicity. Now, I\'m reviewing the required login UI, including the full-screen light background, centered white card, and the logo, now considering using the letter \'C\' to match the app\'s identity, or copying the image as requested.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 758366557
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
