    thinking: "**Analyzing the Main View**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focused on redesigning the main application view post-login based on the provided screenshot. The key components seem to be the top header, which is the immediate priority. I\'m noting the \"IG\" logo, and the header copy \"IG CWK Quality assurance\" \"GRADING & MODER\". I\'m also considering the color of the \"IG\" icon, and whether or not to include a logo instead. I\'m focusing on the overall layout and visual flow.\n\n\n**Revising the New Layout**\n\nI\'m now revising the layout based on the upload screen design. The header now includes a folder icon, moon icon for dark mode, an exit button, and a status box. I\'m focusing on the main content area, including the \"CWK UPLOAD ENTRY\" bar, toggle options for single or comparison analyses, and a status pill. I\'m incorporating the form fields for forename, surname, and preferred name, along with the submission type toggle. Finally, I\'m integrating the large dropzone area for CWK uploads. I\'m considering how this fits with the overall app.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Workflow**\n\nOkay, the multi-screen flow is becoming clearer, as there\'s a sequence: Login, Upload (the screenshot), then Analysis Results. It seems the \"Professional Polish\" design might apply to the moderation/analysis results screen, and I need to determine how the upload screen integrates. I need to clarify if the upload screen is *the* primary view, before the moderation view, or if it is just a step to moderation.\n\n\n**Designing the Upload View**\n\nOkay, I\'m now structuring the application flow. My updated plan includes using the new upload page as the primary post-login view. Then, upon upload, we\'ll transition to the evaluation screen, which is currently the main content of `App.tsx`. I\'m restructuring `App.tsx` with `isLoggedIn` and `appState` states to manage transitions. The upload screen will have a shared header and a container with form fields and a drag-and-drop area. I am confident in this direction.\n\n\n**Implementing File Upload**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the file upload feature within the upload view. Initially, I\'ll create a large, dashed-border drop zone with an upload icon and a \"Click to upload...\" prompt. I\'ve noted that the UI specifies PDF-only uploads. While the backend currently handles text, I\'ll install `pdf-parse` to accommodate this. To get things moving, I\'ll simulate a text upload to the \"Moderation\" view until that screen is designed, and the file upload functionality is complete.\n\n\n**Constructing the Upload View**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `UploadView.tsx`, which will be the default post-login view. I\'m focusing on the dropzone\'s behavior, which will initially set a file state. I\'ll integrate it into `App.tsx`. The design\'s color adjustments have been clarified: I\'m swapping the green accents in the screenshot with blue to match the rest of the app. This includes the logo, text, and buttons. I\'ve started the header layout with a blue background, white \"IG\" logo, and the title in blue text.\n\n\n**Defining the Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now detailing the individual visual components. The header will use a blue title and subtext. The right side includes buttons for folder and moon icons, along with an exit button and a status box. I\'m noting the main card\'s styling, and its header with file icon, title, and toggle group. I am still considering their roles, but have a detailed visual structure.\n\n\n**Styling the Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the component styles for the upload view form. I\'m focusing on the \"ARE 2 CWKs\" badge, which I will render as a small, bold, gray text badge. The \"Ready\" badge will use a blue background and text, as indicated. The card body includes three columns for the form fields, with labels styled with a red asterisk and inputs, that have a border with a rounded appearance. I am ensuring that the Submission Type toggle group follows the styling guide as well. Finally, I\'ll style the dropzone with a dashed border, upload icon, and text prompt.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 19
      nanos: 693529702
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
