  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Local Save**\n\nI\'m now implementing the three-step local save process within `ModerationResults.tsx`, using a modal wizard as requested. The primary goal is to archive the assessment data. For this initial phase, I\'ll leverage standard local state rather than integrating with a backend, focusing on delivering the requested ability to create classes and assignments without persistent storage.\n\n\n**Designing Modal Wizard**\n\nI\'ve outlined the three steps for the archive assessment modal, mapping the required inputs. Step one includes candidate identity and submission type selection. Step two focuses on class and assignment selection with dropdowns and add buttons. Finally, step three presents a summary. I\'ll integrate the \"Save To Directory\" button to trigger this wizard.\n\n\n**Refining Styling Implementation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the modal state into `ModerationResults` and creating the `ArchiveModal.tsx` component. I\'ve paused briefly to restore the original green/teal color (`#00bda5`) for visual consistency, as per user requests. This involves re-integrating the style for the modal buttons and accents.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 70
      nanos: 303488371
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_CLIENT_INVALID_MESSAGE_ORDER
  }
}
