    started_at {
      seconds: 1779629337
      nanos: 836661328
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refactoring UI Colors**\n\nI\'m currently updating the color scheme within `ArchiveModal.tsx`. The goal is to replace the hardcoded accent color `#00bda5` with Tailwind CSS\'s blue variants. I\'m evaluating the usage of each instance to determine if `blue-600`, `blue-500`, or even `blue-100` is the most appropriate replacement, ensuring a consistent and maintainable design. So far, I\'ve identified several `text-[#00bda5]` instances which I intend to switch to `text-blue-600` or `text-blue-500`, depending on the context.\n\n\n**Analyzing Color Consistency**\n\nI\'ve been examining the color consistency across several components. The initial focus on `ArchiveModal.tsx` and replacing the hardcoded accent color has expanded to include `ModerationResults.tsx` and `UploadView.tsx`. I\'m systematically replacing `#00bda5` with `blue-600` or its variations based on context and style. Also, I realized that the folder icon on `UploadView.tsx` needs to link to a directory. I\'m taking the prompt into account, so that means the colors should match.\n\n\n**Implementing Directory Feature**\n\nI\'m now integrating the directory functionality. I\'ve decided to add a new state, `\'directory\'`, to `appState` in `App.tsx` and am creating the `DirectoryView.tsx` component. This component will be where the directory interface is housed. I envision it as a navigable area for folder creation. I\'m focusing on the design principles of the example user interface, to ensure that the user can create and navigate the folders.\n\n\n**Evaluating Color Strategy**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a more efficient way to handle color replacements. Initially, I thought about using `sed`, but realized a more robust approach is needed given the scope of the changes. I\'m exploring an inline script using `npx` with a TypeScript file, as this seems the best method to update multiple files. This will address the color consistency issue in `ModerationResults.tsx`, `ArchiveModal.tsx`, and `LoadingView.tsx` by replacing the specified hex codes and green accents with the appropriate blue variants.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 948207766
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
