    thinking: "**Verifying Prompt Style Consistency**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the styling discrepancy is resolved between the two prompts, I used \"IG\" and a blue accent. I am now working on ensuring the login page mirrors the specified design, complete with the logo and name in the top left corner.\n\n\n**Checking Execute Button State**\n\nI\'ve validated that the execute button in the upload view is correctly greyed out when no coursework is selected and turns blue on selection, as confirmed by the CSS. Dark mode toggle functionality is confirmed.\n\n\n**Adapting Criteria Display**\n\nI\'m now adapting the display of student feedback to match the IG standards. This involves translating the IAQA and TEACHER scoring to IGQA and TEACHER, and using a 1-5 scale instead of A-F. I\'m focusing on the visual layout and ensuring the \"reset moderator\" and \"save to directory\" options are correctly implemented, mirroring the desired functionality.\n\n\n**Confirming Save Process Functionality**\n\nI\'ve verified that the \"save to directory\" function triggers the expected three-step process, as visualized in the provided screenshots. The `ArchiveModal.tsx` component is correctly handling the creation of classes and assignments, including a dropdown for assigning graded uploads to existing ones. The logic for `isAddingClass` and `isAddingAssignment` within the modal confirms this. The save to directory process should be complete.\n\n\n**Developing Directory Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the DirectoryView component, enabling navigation through Classes, Assignments, and Students. The directory will display IGQA and TEACHER scores for each student. I\'m prioritizing the \"Draft vs Final\" comparison, ensuring the final report juxtaposes drafts and finals, with editable TEACHER criteria. I\'m still figuring out how to handle the upload of the Final CWK.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 662522520
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
