  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Import Structure**\n\nI\'ve confirmed `motion` is installed and successfully imported from `\'motion/react\'`. Now, I\'m focusing on incorporating this into `DirectoryView.tsx` to handle folder addition and swipe-to-delete functionalities. The necessary import statements are in place.\n\n\n**Implementing Swipe Interaction**\n\nI\'m now building the `SwipeableFolder` component. My plan involves a delete button revealed upon swiping left, avoiding complex state management. I will use a `motion.div` from `framer-motion` for the swipe interaction and am making a background for the delete button. The component structure and import structure is starting to come together.\n\n\n**Constructing Animation Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating animation using `framer-motion` for swipe interactions within a `SwipeableItem` component. I\'ve defined animation controls and implemented drag handling to reveal a delete button upon a leftward swipe. The animation uses offsets to control swipe direction and the controls are managing states. I\'ve integrated a renaming functionality which can be triggered by drag and hold.\n\n\n**Refining Interaction Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating a delete button with a `motion.div`, triggered by a leftward swipe. I\'m focusing on `drag=\"x\"` to control the swipe, with constraints to prevent over-swiping, and onDragEnd to manage the control state. I\'m leveraging `framer-motion` for smooth animations and visually responding to drag events. I\'m fine tuning the control animation using offsets and a conditional component render, for a cleaner UI.\n\n\n**Integrating Rename Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the renaming feature within the swipeable item. I\'ve integrated an input field that appears when a user triggers renaming, and reverts to the folder name on blur or escape. I\'ve set up event listeners for `Enter` and `Escape` keys to streamline interaction and prevent the renaming from persisting if it is abandoned. I\'m also now linking the input value with state to update it dynamically, and have disabled renaming within the drag interactions for a smoother UX.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 550030447
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
