  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Directory View**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting an accordion directory for the user. My current concern centers on clarity: the user needs a prominent \"Add Teacher Folder\" option. Once a class folder is expanded, I envision seeing either \"No assignments\" or a \"+ ADD SUBFOLDER\" button for assignment organization. This design aims for intuitive folder and assignment management.\n\n\n**Refining the Directory UI**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI updates. I need to integrate renamable and deletable assignment subfolders with edit and trash icons within the accordion view. I\'ll need to revisit the existing delete function, checking `deleteClass` and `deleteAssignment`, as the user mentioned it\'s not working. The key will be ensuring that the user can rename and delete either the subfolder or assignments with the click of an icon.\n\n\n**Implementing the Class Row**\n\nI\'m now implementing the class row UI in `DirectoryView.tsx`. It needs a Chevron, Folder icon, Name, Edit icon, and Trash icon. My priority is to first ensure that the `deleteClass` and `deleteAssignment` functions in `db.ts` are working correctly. It seems like the issue isn\'t the deletion itself, but the `refreshData()` function not updating the UI after deletion. This needs further debugging.\n\n\n**Simplifying the UI**\n\nI\'ve decided to scrap `SwipeableItem` and directly implement \"Edit\" and \"Trash\" buttons on the folder items, to match the user\'s screenshot. I\'m rebuilding the sidebar to improve the user experience. This means the sidebar will consist of a \"Master Directory\" header, and an \"Add Teacher Folder\" button. I will refactor the folder display to utilize a unified `classes` data object.\n\n\n**Refactoring the Directory Logic**\n\nI\'m now restructuring the core logic for class and assignment management. I\'m focusing on a more efficient approach to data structuring and retrieval, consolidating class and assignment data. I\'m leveraging `useState` to manage class expansion and creating components like `ClassFolder` and potentially an `AccordionFolder`. I also need to ensure consistent styling of the input components for new class names. I\'m currently refactoring `DirectoryView.tsx` to streamline the user interface.\n\n\n**Combining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how `assignmentsForClass` needs to combine data structures. I\'m ensuring it accounts for both structure data and assignment data. I\'m also preparing the sidebar UI elements. I\'m prioritizing the layout and styling, including the \"Master Directory\" header and the \"Add Teacher Folder\" button, to enhance the user experience.\n\n\n**Implementing the \"Add Teacher Folder\"**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Add Teacher Folder\" button and input field. I am making this a key part of the new sidebar design. I will manage the visibility of the input field using `isCreatingClass`, and handle class creation with the `createClass` function. I also need to use `refreshData()` function to refresh the directory data after actions.\n\n\n**Refining the Class Accordion**\n\nI\'m working on the `ClassAccordion` component now. I\'m focusing on creating an accordion UI to display class-specific assignments. I\'m integrating the ability to expand and collapse, manage assignment states and implementing assignment operations such as add, delete, and rename. I\'m thinking about renaming and subfolder creation as well.\n\n\n**Enhancing the Edit Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the edit functionality within the accordion. I\'m focusing on handling the renaming process, specifically integrating an edit button. I\'ve designed the Edit2 icon and cancel function, and added it to the accordion component. My immediate goal is a smooth transition from a display name to an editable input field.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Assignment Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final UI components for assignment management. I\'ve built in the delete functionality and the \"no assignments\" message. I\'m focusing on the state management for adding assignments and implementing the `NewFolderInput` functionality. I\'ll need to link that to the right functions to complete the assignment edit process.\n\n\n\n**Adding Subfolder Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the subfolder addition within the accordion, including its conditional rendering. I\'m focusing on the `NewFolderInput` integration, which I\'ve included with an `onSubmit` and `onCancel` function. I am also working on rendering the Add Subfolder button, along with implementing the `ChevronDown` icon. I\'m also ready to implement a refined `AssignmentItem`.\n\n\n**Finalizing the UI**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final UI components, specifically adding icons for Edit and Trash, within the accordion. I am focusing on assignment management, and subfolder creation and delete. I\'ve designed the visual cues for assignment actions. I\'ve also focused on the rendering of the subfolder functionality and associated states.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Color Scheme**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a refined UI. The recent update involves harmonizing the color scheme. I\'ve updated the folder input to align with the application\'s green color, specifically using `text-green-600` and `text-red-500` for color consistency. I\'ve also integrated the `AssignmentItem` to stop propagation on the buttons to improve interactions. I\'m focusing on the input components\' aesthetics.\n\n\n**Addressing the Deselection**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the assignment selection logic within the `DirectoryView` component. My focus is on the `selectedAssignment` state; I need to confirm whether re-clicking an open assignment deselects it, providing a clean UI behavior. This is crucial for user navigation.\n\n\n\n**Revising Pane Structures**\n\nI\'m now restructuring the UI panes to accommodate new interactions. I\'ve realized the need for a dedicated pane to display student details once an assignment is selected. I need to make the selections from the class, then to assignments and students. I\'m clarifying how each selection unfolds into the student display, ensuring the accordion flows logically. I\'m focusing on the logical order of operations and interactions.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the relationship between the accordion and the student display. I\'m visualizing the three levels: Class -> Assignment -> Students. My understanding is that the left sidebar will act as the accordion, offering a three-level drill-down. When I select an assignment, the middle pane will display the student list, and clicking a student will update the report in the right pane. I\'m focusing on user flow clarity.\n\n\n\n**Restructuring the UI**\n\nI\'m now restructuring the UI to integrate a three-pane layout for class, assignment, and student data. The accordion will reside in a sidebar. Selecting an assignment in the sidebar will populate the middle pane with student listings. Clicking a student will then display the report in the rightmost pane. The current `DirectoryView` structure needs adjustments.\n\n\n**Implementing the Three-Pane UI**\n\nI\'m now implementing the three-pane layout in `DirectoryView`, creating dedicated columns for the classes/assignments accordion, student listings, and student detail views. I\'m focusing on the layout and responsiveness using the provided Tailwind classes to ensure a clear flow from class selection to student evaluation. The structure is: a sidebar for the accordion, a middle pane for students, and a right pane for student reports.\n\n\n\n**Refining the UI Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the components for teacher folder addition. The button, including the \'+\' icon and the \"New Folder Input\", are now implemented. I also focused on managing `isCreatingClass`, using the `createClass` and `refreshData` functions. The styling is also ready. I need to make sure the user flow makes sense.\n\n\n**Updating the Directory**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data and logic for assignment management. I\'ve updated the `DirectoryView` component with functions for creating, deleting, and renaming assignments. These functions are linked to data refreshing and UI updates. I\'ve focused on syncing the selection logic for assignments and classes, handling state management for each.\n\n\n**Integrating Student Views**\n\nI\'m now integrating the student list into the middle pane, triggered by assignment selection. The layout includes class and assignment headers above the student list and conditional messaging for no submissions. I\'m dynamically generating the students\' list from the `studentsForAssignment` data, with a focus on seamless selection and interaction flow. I\'m focusing on ensuring student selection triggers the student detail view.\n\n\n**Refining the Student Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the student display logic. I\'ve updated the UI to clearly show the student\'s status with an icon indicating completion. I\'m focusing on dynamic list generation and ensuring student selection updates the report in the right pane. I\'m also ensuring the styling is clear and aligns with the existing UI framework.\n\n\n**Integrating the Detail Pane**\n\nI\'m now integrating the student detail view pane. I\'m dynamically rendering either the student details or a placeholder message based on user selection. I\'ve focused on ensuring the student details pane is correctly populated with the right information. I\'ve also incorporated the folder icon and messaging for no student details.\n\n\n**Managing Directory Expansion**\n\nI\'m now integrating the expanded state for classes in `DirectoryView`. I\'ll use `[expandedClass, setExpandedClass]` at the top level, to handle initial expansion of freshly added classes. I\'m preparing to rewrite `DirectoryView.tsx` with all the new components and I am also preparing to use `edit_file` to replace the existing content. I\'ll read the code first to understand the structure.\n\n\n"
