  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising Layout Strategy**\n\nI\'m currently focused on refactoring the `src/components/DirectoryView.tsx` file. Specifically, I plan to overwrite lines 329 to 441 to implement a new layout. This involves a `main` element with `flex-1` and `p-6` classes to expand and add padding. I\'m also implementing a sidebar that contains the navigation for classes and assignments. I\'ll make sure to add gap and flex-col classes. I am adding a \"search bar\" and buttons as well.\n\n\n**Adding Directory Hierarchy**\n\nI\'ve been working on the directory structure within the sidebar. I\'ve added a container with `overflow-y-auto` to handle content overflow. There\'s also a \"Master Directory\" header with a green folder icon. I\'ve included a button that triggers the class creation input, and I\'m using `NewFolderInput` for this, also implementing a cancel and refresh functionality upon creation.\n\n\n**Implementing Class Accordions**\n\nI\'m now integrating class accordions within the directory sidebar, using a `flex flex-col gap-2 pb-10` layout. Each accordion is rendered for a class, managing its expansion state, name, and interactions. I have set up `onToggle` for expansion, `onRename` and `onDelete` to handle class management, and `onAddAssignment`, `onDeleteAssignment`, and `onRenameAssignment` for assignment operations. I\'m dynamically displaying assignments associated with each class, ensuring data integrity across different data sources.\n\n\n**Refining Assignment Interaction**\n\nI\'m currently working on the middle pane which displays the students. I\'ve integrated interaction with the assignment panel, so I\'m focusing on the logic to display and manage student submissions based on the selected class and assignment. I\'m making sure that the data updates seamlessly when a new selection is made, with careful consideration for edge cases, such as when there are no students or no submissions.\n\n\n**Displaying Student Submissions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the student submission display within the main pane. This includes a conditional rendering based on available submissions, showing \"No submissions yet\" when appropriate. I\'m dynamically generating buttons for each student, setting their appearance based on submission status, and highlighting the selected student. The buttons are interactive, setting the selected student on click, and managing the display and interaction logic of student submission details.\n\n\n**Finalizing Submission Display**\n\nI\'m now completing the student submission display logic. The plan is to enhance the presentation of each student\'s details using `renderStudentDetails`. I\'ve added a conditional rendering that shows either a \"Select a candidate\" message or the candidate\'s detailed evaluation. The structure is implemented with the `Folder` icon, and proper font and text styling. Now, I will ensure smooth interaction and display when there are no submissions.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 28
      nanos: 968600852
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
