  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Directory Behavior**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the master directory\'s rename function. It seems counterintuitive that renaming clears the existing name field; it should persist for modification. I\'m trying to determine the logic behind this behavior and how to retain the current name as a default suggestion.\n\n\n**Confirming Recent Fix**\n\nI realized the recent fix in `NewFolderInput` addresses the rename issue directly. The introduction of `initialValue` and its integration with `useState` now preserves the name during renaming operations, resolving the blank name display problem that existed prior. I\'ve confirmed that this fix is now live, after an initial local compilation.\n\n\n"
