    thinking: "**Refining Upload Logic**\n\nOkay, so I\'m thinking about the upload restriction. Initially, I was focusing on enabling/disabling the upload function itself, basically `handleFileUpload`. But now, I\'m leaning toward the idea of simply hiding the file input field entirely until the necessary name fields are filled. It seems a cleaner approach.\n\n\n**Considering UI Improvements**\n\nI\'m now thinking about UI/UX improvements to the upload process. Instead of just disabling, I\'m going to disable the dropzone when the required name fields are empty. Also, I\'ll disable the \"Execute Moderation\" button, for consistency. I\'ve updated `handleFileUpload` to include this logic. I will also clear the file input after preventing upload.\n\n\n**Implementing Conditional Disabling**\n\nI\'ve decided to refine the approach further. Instead of the potentially confusing `cursor-not-allowed` style, I will conditionally disable the file input element. This will rely on the required form fields, namely `forename`, `surname`, and `preferredName`, and I will control the `disabled` attribute directly. This should provide a more intuitive user experience.\n\n\n**Enhancing Visual Feedback**\n\nI\'m now focusing on providing better visual cues. I\'ve updated the upload button text to \"Please fill all name fields first\" if the name fields are empty, and \"Click to upload candidate CWK\" otherwise. The text color also changes to provide additional feedback. I\'ve also implemented conditional disabling for the \"Execute Moderation\" button, ensuring it\'s grayed out until a file is selected and all name fields are complete.\n\n\n"
